#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:3
#: 9b6999bccb28440a82397c9c5224a5dd
msgid "How to use devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:5
#: 7d479f22d3094c72881f93eda1f653bb
msgid ""
"This is an overview of device handling in Qubes OS. For specific devices "
"(:doc:`block </user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-block-storage-"
"devices>`, :doc:`USB </user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-usb-devices>` "
"and :doc:`PCI </user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-pci-devices>` devices), please "
"visit their respective pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:7
#: 86f5d1d79a8541fca2e1db8b2008f9f5
msgid ""
"**Important security warning:** Device handling comes with many security "
"implications. Please make sure you carefully read and understand "
"the :doc:`security considerations </user/security-in-qubes/device-handling-"
"security>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:10
#: 25ea6f87292a414cbc9422427407cdd9
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:12
#: e22304a11b054433bb9acc4dd83e435e
msgid ""
"The interface to deal with devices of all sorts was unified in Qubes 4.0 "
"with the ``qvm-device`` command and the :guilabel:`Qubes Devices widget`. In "
"Qubes 3.X, the Qubes VM Manager dealt with attachment as well. This "
"functionality was moved to the :guilabel:`Qubes Devices widget`, the tool "
"tray icon with a USB trident symbol located in the top right of your screen "
"by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:14
#: 557e366c8b2840f88d848a185a26126c
msgid "There are currently four categories of devices Qubes understands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:16
#: 16442ec7e78242be85d523cbf45828af
msgid "Microphones"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:18
#: 96aacf08e51f4c07a62fb861f1925faa
msgid "Block devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:20
#: ba7e363bbe704fccb52b3ad66ea71032
msgid "USB devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:22
#: 7dd0a91a6d7f4d0e96379e1e182fba9d
msgid "PCI devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:24
#: 3c13d311939146f19079eee27739f68a
msgid ""
"Microphones, block devices and USB devices can be attached with the GUI-"
"tool. PCI devices can be attached using the Qube Settings, but require a VM "
"reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:27
#: 185507cca9984f9c8d634b90a75170ae
msgid "General Qubes Devices Widget Behavior And Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:34
#: 2fd818a871c343ad91298e8e07171b5e
msgid "Qubes Devices widget tray icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:36
#: 4287af61d93b44759a708875c6e91c65
msgid ""
"When clicking on the tray icon, several device-classes separated by lines "
"are displayed as tooltip. Block devices are displayed on top, microphones "
"one below and USB-devices at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:38
#: 75f9b9686498479a845aab713e938295
msgid ""
"On most laptops, integrated hardware such as cameras and fingerprint-readers "
"are implemented as USB-devices and can be found here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:45
#: fcb9218d721d4181920fbfbdcff013f8
msgid "Attaching Using The Widget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:47
#: 95ec2a3a4f1745f6af3462c13a79ce6a
msgid ""
"Click the tray icon. Hover on a device you want to attach to a VM. A list of "
"running VMs (except dom0) appears. Click on one and your device will be "
"attached!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:50
#: 5d59f349205946498630dbd8fd887d58
msgid "Detaching Using The Widget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:52
#: e835d97c28704e23b05e6fcc4893a693
msgid ""
"To detach a device, click the :guilabel:`Qubes Devices widget` icon again. "
"Attached devices are displayed in bold. Hover the one you want to detach. A "
"list of VMs appears, one showing the eject symbol: |eject icon|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:147
#: 767f4d520d024404bc549d06b8534675
msgid "eject icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:55
#: 9a63b42d6a164fbe80404ea6ba2e9776
msgid "Attaching a Device to Several VMs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:57
#: 2a3e2cefaea142ddb35a2fc7c5c41995
msgid ""
"Only ``mic`` should be attached to more than one running VM. You may "
"*assign* a device to more than one VM (using the ``--persistent`` option), "
"however, only one of them can be started at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:60
#: 7f3404e877474d5a854244a85a66d323
msgid "General ``qvm-device`` Command Line Tool Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:62
#: c41cfd3177c54f4ba760b8280cd0416b
msgid ""
"All devices, including PCI-devices, may be attached from the commandline "
"using the ``qvm-device``-tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:65
#: 942f01ad51a24a53990ac6689570c750
msgid "Device Classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:67
#: a36b0f867f8446aca4358be93cc12a49
msgid ""
"``qvm-device`` expects DEVICE_CLASS as first argument. DEVICE_CLASS can be "
"one of"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:69
#: 2fb8fde71dfd4137af719901b6eae567
msgid "``pci``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:71
#: 63e0e94878f44798931d0f5d32eb86e5
msgid "``usb``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:73
#: a3dde0423bb74be59e49ba453e62610a
msgid "``block``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:75
#: 519b21c342324ed8a9bfb39f8f2ebd0f
msgid "``mic``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:78
#: fc344991c7ae4f81885f7154845022e8
msgid "``qvm-device`` Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:80
#: 598773ab553b415e97551e5aeb35d0c8
msgid "``qvm-device`` supports three actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:82
#: 69f386f9cdbc4ed6a114d955e5fab74b
msgid "``list`` (ls, l) - list all devices of DEVICE_CLASS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:84
#: 7cad047ebef640fb8ab6832d11822719
msgid "``attach`` (at, a) - attach a specific device of DEVICE_CLASS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:86
#: a32660b84fef4999bc382070d810cfb4
msgid "``detach`` (dt, d) - detach a specific device of DEVICE_CLASS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:89
#: 2fc1af5c29a94dd6bff4b2dcb16d37bd
msgid "Global Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:91
#: ecb7458252b94ff2b0061c34bd59f845
msgid "These three options are always available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:93
#: b1cb22a385784397bc271bce998c7859
msgid "``--help``, ``-h`` - show help message and exit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:95
#: 93a6fc04cf114e899a4d4c027601ecab
msgid "``--verbose``, ``-v`` - increase verbosity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:97
#: 98e326c683fa4990a4c14a0b0e204954
msgid "``--quiet``, ``-q`` - decrease verbosity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:99
#: 655740adfa8042a5972a2b5faf96f6c9
msgid ""
"A full command consists of one DEVICE_CLASS and one action. If no action is "
"given, list is implied. DEVICE_CLASS however is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:101
#: 0971a31075444151ac22a6825d2ebf64
msgid ""
"**SYNOPSIS**: ``qvm-device DEVICE_CLASS {action} [action-specific arguments] "
"[options]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:106
#: bf88d7332dac47ffa2338de63f3f3795
msgid "Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:108
#: 7688021a98da4cb98ce71ed4e78f2272
msgid ""
"Actions are applicable to every DEVICE_CLASS and expose some additional "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:111
#: 8f9032a294d249eab46bef1f38f9a413
msgid "Listing Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:113
#: 2c0cf30958bb4bfbabad86b6c83f7385
msgid ""
"The ``list`` action lists known devices in the system. ``list`` accepts VM-"
"names to narrow down listed devices. Devices available in, as well as "
"attached to the named VMs will be listed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:115
#: 246d6d9cdc0844db88737b14b3f9b147
msgid "``list`` accepts two options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:117
#: 2763a04a3fb1441282f5b3e292d0ad6b
msgid ""
"``--all`` - equivalent to specifying every VM name after ``list``. No VM-"
"name implies ``--all``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:119
#: 7f028063003c4d69a1bd68fc9cf6fc55
msgid "``--exclude`` - exclude VMs from ``--all``. Requires ``--all``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:121
#: 40404d1fe5b14cd895abf9160e8ed585
msgid ""
"**SYNOPSIS** ``qvm-device DEVICE_CLASS {list|ls|l} [--all [--exclude VM [VM "
"[...]]] | VM [VM [...]]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:124
#: a88847bc93e740db9009f2e45517a445
msgid "Attaching Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:126
#: 2e74537e46294f0aac1a977d26f58997
msgid ""
"The ``attach`` action assigns an exposed device to a VM. This makes the "
"device available in the VM it’s attached to. Required argument are targetVM "
"and sourceVM:deviceID. (sourceVM:deviceID can be determined from ``list`` "
"output)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:128
#: 481f13904a9f47ca804125c311c67cd1
msgid "``attach`` accepts two options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:130
#: 9cef3f9dbe9745eda2dcba1a8be7fa41
msgid ""
"``--persistent`` - attach device on targetVM-boot. If the device is "
"unavailable (physically missing or sourceVM not started), booting the "
"targetVM fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:132
#: 8ded2cf08a35487bb114fd1f84301f8d
msgid "``--option``, ``-o`` - set additional options specific to DEVICE_CLASS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:134
#: 595d40991be2489a9dd52a7837a0812e
msgid ""
"**SYNOPSIS** ``qvm-device DEVICE_CLASS {attach|at|a} targetVM "
"sourceVM:deviceID [options]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:137
#: 0a720f53e1dd44e0882bd85440be55b0
msgid "Detaching Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:139
#: 4ed8bacba57e4c9cbc0089c1d4737e19
msgid ""
"The ``detach`` action removes an assigned device from a targetVM. It won’t "
"be available afterwards anymore. Though it tries to do so gracefully, beware "
"that data-connections might be broken unexpectedly, so close any transaction "
"before detaching a device!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:141
#: 3a044cd357aa4993a39b0510d7b470f1
msgid ""
"If no specific ``sourceVM:deviceID`` combination is given, *all devices of "
"that DEVICE_CLASS will be detached.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:143
#: 7b00a78803e8403096a5f9d85e739f46
msgid "``detach`` accepts no options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-devices.rst:145
#: 82a67bf588ea491dada2cdee1872faf6
msgid ""
"**SYNOPSIS** ``qvm-device DEVICE_CLASS {detach|dt|d} targetVM "
"[sourceVM:deviceID]``"
msgstr ""
